cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: "vlm-cpu-benchmark: A Fair CPU-Only Efficiency and Quantization Benchmark for Small Vision-Language Models"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible, CPU-only benchmarking framework for small vision-language
  models. It separates pre-processing, inference, and post-processing latency
  and reports peak memory and best-effort RAPL energy under fixed hardware,
  resolution, and token budgets, across fp32 and custom ONNX INT8 backends, on
  DocVQA, OCRBench, and a shared object-presence task that also compares the
  VLMs against CPU object detectors in closed- and open-vocabulary regimes.
type: software
